      "translations": {
        "en": "I asked Abu Abdillah and Abu al-Hasan (peace be upon him) about a woman who committed adultery, so she gave birth to a child, and she confessed in the presence of the Imam of the Muslims that she had committed adultery and that this child of hers was from the adultery. So the Hadd (penalty) was established upon her. And that child grew up until he became a man. So a man fabricated against him [accusation of adultery]. Would the one who fabricated against him be whipped? He (peace be upon him) said: 'He would be whipped, and he would not be whipped.' So I said: 'How can he be whipped and not be whipped?'"
